      "id": "java4shell",
      "cve": "CVE-2026-114938",
      "title": "Java4Shell: memory corruption in the OpenJDK Base64 decoder, remote code execution",
      "severity": "critical",
      "severity_note": "Red Hat rates it Critical (CVSS 3.0 9.8), Ubuntu High (CVSS 3.1 8.1); the NVD has not scored it yet.",
      "condition": "Affects only x86-64 processors with AVX-512 VBMI; ARM64 is not affected. The collector does not report CPU features yet, so every x86-64 host with an affected build is listed; java -Xlog:os+cpu=info -version shows whether the JVM sees avx512_vbmi.",
      "mitigation": "Update to the vendor's fixed build. Until then start the JVM with -XX:-UseBASE64Intrinsics (for example through JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS) and restart the service; -XX:UseAVX=2 also works on x86-64 but stops an ARM64 JVM from starting. A mitigation is not a fix.",
      "references": [
